>1) If I name my weapon to the name of special weapons (artifacts), will
>   that help? I named a two-handed sword to Orcrist (happened to get a list
>   of the names of artifacts), it worked. But if I named something else,
>   like long sword, axe or orcish dagger, it didn't work. It ended up an 
>   altered name.

Naming weapons yourself will work on two accounts only (you have found one).
Named weapons are infact better than its unnamed counterpart, for one thing,
they may do special damage to certain kinds of monsters....like any of the
..banes. Many of them receive extra Hit bonuses, and some have extra
Damage bonuses as well. Some will even offer some special defenses...check
out the brands.
>
>2) Weapons seem very cheap compare to other items. Are they not important in
>   this game? I played moria, an ego weapon is one of the most important items
>   there.

The prices of the weapons are generally based upon the price list in AD&D.
named weapons are much more expensive.
>
>3) Are the characters about the same? If not, which is better? I switch 
>   between Barbarian, Samuri and Valkyrie. Wizard is fun to play. 
>   Knight and Rogue seem wimpy to me, am I right? What is the good of 
>   Archeologist and Tourist?
>
All characters are different in that they begin with different items, stats,
and intrinsics. Samuries and priests have the extra ability to effectively
kick the living daylights out of monsters and boxes. Archeologist is a
challenging character who can automatically identify gems for you, like
a wizard he's very intelligent.

Got any food problems? try out a tourist.

